    },
    "message": "Share the parsed facility geometry and spatial constraints within a phase\n\nTick phases parse the facility geometry once per raw config through\ngeometry_config_scope, but several callers still parsed it themselves,\nand movement parsed the spatial constraints again at every call (#45).\nIts _spatial_constraints returned the effective constraints as a JSON\ndump, and route_is_physically_clear, plan_in_room_route, queue slots and\nfacility approaches each validated that dump into a new model.\n\n_spatial_constraints now returns the effective SpatialConstraints model\nitself. It is built from validated walls, obstacles and footprints and\nSpatialConstraints has no model-wide validator, so the dump parsed again\nwas an equal model. The new parsed_facility_geometry returns the\nScenario's geometry without runtime overrides and, inside a config\nscope, shares the parse effective_geometry uses. Facility queues, the\noperational demand snapshot, runner routes, population arrivals and the\narrival effect check use it; outside a scope it parses at each call as\nbefore.\n\nFor 100 people the world, events and metrics hashes equal those before\nthe change over 360 and 1440 minutes of the generated Scenario and 360\nminutes of the 100-person fixture Scenario.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
